    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d483-a4">

                <pb facs="0654" n="548" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg548"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The minister of foreign affairs of
                            the Dominican Republic to Mr. Dawson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Dominican Republic,<lb/>Ministry of Foreign Relations</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1906-01-12"><hi rendition="#italic">January
                                12, 1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: In reply to your excellency’s note
                    of this date, I have to inform you that the Government is willing to concede
                    permission to go abroad to the citizens Carlos F. Morales, Enrique Jiminez, and
                    Gregorio Encarnacion, they to reside there until something else is determined
                    upon.</p>
                <p>I approve, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Tejera.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
